What is in which build
----------------------

The obligations scale with what you compile in, which is why
`chapbook-reader`'s format features are separable:

    chapbook-panel-fbdev alone
        nothing beyond MIT/Apache-2.0.

    chapbook-reader --no-default-features
        + MPL-2.0 (stylo), Apache-2.0 (rbook, unicode-linebreak),
          BSD-3-Clause (tiny-skia), Unicode-3.0 (ICU4X).

    chapbook-reader (default: cbz, pdf, opds)
        + ring, webpki-roots, brotli, subtle, alloc-*.

    chapbook-opds --no-default-features
        none of the TLS set. The whole licence surface above belongs to
        the bundled `ureq` transport rather than to OPDS itself, so a
        build that injects its own `HttpClient` keeps catalogs and sheds
        all of it. Not yet reachable through chapbook-reader, which still
        constructs `OpdsClient::with_ureq()` directly.

    chapbook-viewer / chapbook-viewer-gtk
        + the winit and wgpu Apache-2.0 set, dpi, hexf-parse.

